    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** headlining the roster as our most efficient starts, scoring 73.66 and 73.00, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Wacha, where a high base projection is compounded by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** remains an elite play not only for his high scoring output but for his aggressive stolen base upside; the slow delivery of Pallante offers a rare secondary boost that keeps him locked in as an essential cornerstone of our 5x5 strategy. **Drake Baldwin** also warrants a mention for his high-ceiling score of 69.17, driven by a leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Houser.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Gunnar Henderson** on the bench despite his elite pedigree. While **Gunnar Henderson** projects reasonably well, the optimizer prioritized the platoon and SP-skill advantages of our starting infielders, particularly against a tough arm in Gilbert. We continue to prioritize stolen base potential and favorable matchups, which effectively kept **Nasim Nunez** and **Josh Jung** on the pine today; **Nasim Nunez** simply lacks the favorable order slot to out-produce the high-efficiency daily output of our current starters. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Wade Meckler**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Nolan Schanuel**. Specifically, **Kyle Tucker** is currently skating near our floor with a 54.20 score due to a tough assignment against Rasmussen; if he drops in the order upon official lineup release, we may need to pivot. Furthermore, **Miguel Vargas** faces a formidable task against Gerrit Cole; while he maintains a solid 59.66, the high-strikeout profile of the opposition makes him a volatile piece in today\u2019s construction. Ensure all lineup confirmations are monitored to verify that these projections remain anchored to the actual batting order.",
